-- title:
--   Degeneracy image g(qᵈ) lies in the X_H(N) function field over L
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $M'$ and $d$ be nonzero natural numbers, let $N$ be a natural number with $M'd \mid N$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$. Let $g$ be a formal Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ belonging to [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull M'`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), i.e. to the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series $j(q^{e})$ for the nonzero divisors $e \mid M'$, where $j(q^{e})$ denotes the image of the $j$-expansion `jq` under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{e}$ (realised as the support-rescaling ring homomorphism [`ModularCurve.qExpand`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25)). The conclusion is that the Laurent series over $L$ obtained by first applying $\operatorname{algebraMap}_{\mathbb{Q},L}$ to every coefficient of $g$ (the map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) and then substituting $q \mapsto q^{d}$ lies in [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField N H)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, in the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the elements of $\mathbb{Q}$-function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH N H)`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76) attached to the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H(N)$.
--
--   This is the statement that the degeneracy substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ carries a rational modular function of level $\Gamma_0(M')$, presented by its $q$-expansion, into the function field of $X_H(N)$ whenever $M'd \mid N$, with constants extended from $\mathbb{Q}$ to an arbitrary field of characteristic zero. It is the characteristic-zero-constants form of the corresponding level-$\Gamma_0$ statement and feeds the full-level chart and valuation constructions on modular curves that use explicit $q$-expansions over a general base field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qExpand_coeffEmb_mem_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField_of_mem_modularFunctionFieldFull.lean

